speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I too rise on a question of utmost urgency and importance. The matter relates to a statement made by a leader of the committee representing the Government of Canada in the State of Alaska. The statement by the hon. member for Nipissing (Mr. Blais) was made in reference to hearings held in the State of Alaska on the trans-Canada pipeline route. The hon. member defended a Canadian route to the press which quoted him in a front page report in the Daily News Miner of Fairbanks, Alaska on October 11, 1975 as saying, and I quote:
The native rights have been extinguished in the Northwest Territories;
And further that:
the provinces of Saskatchewan and British Columbia are not controlled by socialist governments;
And that:
foreign investment legislation is not enforced in Canada ...
